4 Sessions
**********

‘M-x harmless-current’
     Open or resume the newest session for this project.  If none
     exists, start one with the default connection and model.

‘M-x harmless-new’
     Start a new session in the current project.  Harmless asks for the
     connection, the model, and the reasoning effort when more than one
     choice exists.

‘M-x harmless-chat’
     Start a chat with no project and no working directory.  This is a
     detached chat.  It can use global memory and ask you a question.
     It cannot read project files, run a shell, or enter plan mode.

‘M-x harmless-switch’
     Jump to a live or saved session.  Completion shows the project, the
     title, and the session id.

‘M-x harmless-dashboard’
     List every session, grouped by project.  *Note Keys::, for the
     dashboard keys.

   The first user message becomes the title, cut at 60 characters, until
you set a title when you create the session.  A set title stays.

   ‘t’, or ‘M-x harmless-rename’, sets the title.  The session id and
its directory stay.  Later prompts do not replace that title.  Nil,
‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘session title is empty’.  A value
that is not text is refused: ‘session title must be a string’.

   ‘x’, or ‘M-x harmless-export-session’, writes the transcript as
Markdown.  The session is not modified.  A relative path stays inside
the project and is not resolved against the buffer's default directory.
An absolute path is written only when its parent already exists.  ‘~’ is
not expanded.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘session export path is
empty’.  A value that is not text is refused: ‘session export path must
be a string’.  A path that names a directory is refused: ‘session export
path is not a file’.  ‘~’ is refused: ‘session export path must be
absolute’.  A relative path outside the project is refused: ‘session
export path escapes the project: ’, followed by the path.  An absolute
path whose parent is missing is refused: ‘session export path is
missing’.  ‘/’ and a drive root are refused: ‘session export path is the
filesystem root’.  A relative path in a detached chat, a blank project,
a relative project, or a project that is the filesystem root is refused
before anything is written.

   ‘X’, or ‘M-x harmless-delete-session’, deletes that session's
directory and drops it from the live list.  An interactive call asks
first.  A turn that is streaming or waiting on permission is refused:
‘session is busy’.  The filesystem root is not a session directory.
Another session's files stay.

   The header line of the transcript shows the title (or the project
name), the connection, the model, the status, and the word ‘plan’ while
plan mode is on.  *Note Plan mode::.

   Two sessions in one project get separate transcript buffers.  The
buffer name is ‘*harmless: PROJECT*’ when the project has one session,
and ‘*harmless: PROJECT ID*’ when it has more.  A detached chat always
includes the id.


