6 Prompt
********

The prompt is a small window under the transcript.  Type there and send
the turn.

‘C-c C-c’
     Send the prompt.  ‘C-c <RET>’ does the same.  While a turn is
     streaming, this queues the prompt instead of aborting the turn.

‘C-c C-a’
     Abort the in-flight turn or shell.  *Note Trouble::.

‘C-c C-k’
     Open the Harmless menu.  *Note Keys::.

   An empty prompt is refused: ‘Prompt is empty’.  Nil, ‘""’, and
whitespace are the same refusal.  While a permission question is
showing, send is refused until you answer it.  *Note Permissions::.

   A prompt can attach context.  ‘@file:PATH’ reads a file.
‘@file:PATH:START-END’ reads a 1-based inclusive line range.
‘@folder:PATH’ lists a directory, at most 200 entries.  ‘@diff’ is the
unstaged diff, ‘@staged’ is the index, and ‘@git:N’ is the last N
commits, from 1 to 10.  ‘@url:URL’ fetches an http or https page.  The
typed text stays, and the attachment follows under ‘--- Attached Context
---’.  A file or folder must stay inside the project or an extra
directory.  An empty reference, a path that leaves the project, and the
filesystem root are refused.  An attachment larger than half the context
window is omitted and the prompt is sent unchanged.  A prompt that
starts with ‘/name’ still loads that skill from the typed text.  The
attachment is built first, so a refused reference does not load the
skill.

   ‘M-x harmless-steer’ reads a follow-up from the minibuffer and queues
it without aborting the turn.  That includes while a permission question
is showing.  The same empty-prompt refusal applies.  A value such as
‘/’, ‘c:/’, or ‘sub/’ is text, and it is queued.

   The follow-up is sent after the current tool batch, before the next
request to the model.  A reply that used no tools is followed by the
queued text, and the turn continues.  Several follow-ups keep the order
they were queued.  Abort drops a queue that has not been sent.


