10 Tools
********

The model does not change your files by printing a diff.  It calls
tools.  You see each call in the transcript.  Permission rules are in
*note Permissions::.

   Tool calls in one reply run together.  Harmless asks for permission
one call at a time.  An allowed call starts before the next question, so
several shell commands overlap.  Results are added to the transcript in
the order the model requested them.  Abort cancels the calls that are
still running.  A review reads the working tree, a base branch, or one
commit and records findings.  It does not edit the project.  *Note
Review::.  ‘lsp’ asks a language server that is already running for a
definition, references, or diagnostics.  *Note Language server::.
‘read_file’ also reads an image, a PDF, and a notebook.  ‘notebook_edit’
replaces one notebook cell.  ‘I’ attaches an image to the next prompt.
*Note File tools::.  ‘skill’ loads one skill into later turns.  *Note
Skills::.  ‘generate_image’ writes a generated image into the project.
*Note Image generation::.  ‘team_boot’, ‘team_inspect’, ‘team_message’,
‘team_snapshot’, and ‘team_restore’ call the same team commands a person
runs.  *Note Team::.

   Paths are relative to the project root unless you pass an absolute
path that is still inside that root, or inside a directory added for
this session.  A path that escapes both is refused.  An empty path is
refused.  The filesystem root is not a project: a search there is
refused, and Harmless will not store its own state there.

   ‘+’, or ‘M-x harmless-add-directory’, lets this session read and edit
one directory outside the project.  The same command is ‘+’ in the
Harmless menu.  The directory is saved with the session.  A fork and a
subagent keep the list.  ‘glob’ searches the project and every added
directory.  With no ‘path’, ‘grep’ does too.  The shell's remembered
directory is still the project only.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘extra directory is empty’.  A
value that is not text is refused: ‘extra directory must be a string’.
A relative path, including ‘~’, is refused and is not expanded: ‘extra
directory must be absolute’.  ‘/’, ‘c:/’, and a drive root are refused:
‘extra directory is the filesystem root’.  A missing path is refused:
‘extra directory is missing’.  A file is refused: ‘extra directory is
not a directory’.  The project itself, and a directory inside it, are
refused: ‘extra directory is inside the project’.  A trailing slash is
the same directory.  A detached chat is refused: ‘This chat is not
attached to a project’.

   A path outside the project and outside every added directory is still
refused: ‘Path escapes project: ’, followed by the path.

   A detached chat is offered ‘memory_read’, ‘memory_remember’,
‘memory_write_topic’, and ‘ask_user’.  *Note Memory::.  *Note
Questions::.  It can list live sessions and send one a finding.  *Note
Messages::.  It can search the web and fetch a page.  *Note Web
search::.  *Note Fetch a page::.  It can search X for posts, a thread,
and accounts.  *Note X search::.  It can list and read MCP resources.
*Note MCP::.  It can see the screen, click, type, and open a browser.
*Note Computer use::.  It can schedule a prompt.  *Note Schedules::.  It
can keep a todo list.  *Note Todos::.

* Menu:

* File tools::  Read, list, write, replace, patch, and notebooks.
* Search::      Find files and lines.
* Shell::       Run a command.
* Questions::   Ask one question with choices.
* Subagents::   A child session that reports a summary.
* Workflows::   One script, many child sessions, one result.
* Worktrees::   Isolated checkouts of the same repository.
* Messages::    A finding sent to another live session.
* Web search::  Look up a query on the web.
* Fetch a page::  Read one http or https page.
* X search::    Find posts, a thread, and accounts on X.
* MCP::         Call a configured server and read its resources.
* Computer use::  See the screen, click, type, and open a browser.
* Monitors::    Wake when a line in a file or a stream matches.
* Schedules::   Send one prompt at a later time.
* Todos::       A list of work with status and dependencies.
* Review::      A read-only review.  Findings are not applied.
* Language server::  Definition, references, and diagnostics.


