10.1 File tools
===============

‘read_file’, ‘list_dir’, ‘write_file’, ‘replace’, and ‘apply_patch’ also
accept a path inside a directory added with ‘M-x
harmless-add-directory’.

‘read_file’
     Read a project file.  ‘offset’ is the first line, counting from 1.
     ‘limit’ is how many lines to return.  Those arguments apply only to
     a text file.  The result is cut at ‘harmless-read-file-max-bytes’
     (100000).  A cut text result ends with ‘[truncated]’.  A read does
     not change the file.

     An image is recognized by its bytes, not by its name.  The result
     is the media type, the path, the byte count, and the bytes.  A file
     larger than the cap is refused: ‘image is too large’.

     A PDF is a file whose name ends in ‘.pdf’.  Harmless reads literal
     strings from the file.  It does not render the page.  A file that
     does not begin with the PDF header is refused: ‘pdf is not a pdf’.
     No literal string is ‘No text’.  A long PDF is cut at the same byte
     cap and ends with ‘[truncated]’.

     A notebook is a file whose name ends in ‘.ipynb’.  The result lists
     each cell.  No cells is ‘No cells’.  A file that is not a notebook
     is refused: ‘notebook is not a notebook’.  A notebook larger than
     the cap is refused: ‘notebook is too large’.

‘notebook_edit’
     Replace the source of one cell in an existing ‘.ipynb’ file.
     ‘path’ is the notebook.  ‘cell’ is a cell id or a 0-based index.
     ‘source’ is the new source.  An empty source clears the cell.
     Other cells stay.  The file is not created.  This is an edit.

     Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace for the path are refused: ‘notebook path
     is empty’.  A value that is not text is refused: ‘notebook path
     must be a string’.  ‘/’, ‘c:/’, and a drive root are refused and
     are not expanded: ‘notebook path is the filesystem root’.  A
     missing notebook is refused: ‘notebook is missing’.  A directory
     and a trailing slash are refused: ‘notebook is not a notebook’.

     A missing cell is refused: ‘notebook cell is empty’.  A value that
     is not a cell id or a 0-based index is refused: ‘notebook cell is
     not a cell’.  No such cell is refused: ‘notebook cell is missing’.
     A missing source is refused: ‘notebook source is empty’.  A value
     that is not text is refused: ‘notebook source must be a string’.

     ‘M-x harmless-attach-image’ queues an image on the next prompt.
     The menu key is ‘I’.  The file must already exist.  Harmless reads
     it and does not change it.  The queue is not saved.  Sending the
     prompt stores the image on that user message.  An empty prompt is
     allowed when an image is queued.  A steer is still text.

     Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘image path is empty’.  A
     value that is not text is refused: ‘image path must be a string’.
     ‘/’, ‘c:/’, and a drive root are refused and are not expanded:
     ‘image path is the filesystem root’.  A relative path in a detached
     chat, and a path that starts with ‘~’, are refused and are not
     expanded: ‘image path must be absolute’.  A missing file is
     refused: ‘image is missing’.  A directory, a trailing slash, and
     bytes that are not an image are refused: ‘image is not an image’.
     A file larger than the cap is refused: ‘image is too large’.

‘list_dir’
     List the names in a directory.  A directory name ends with a slash.
     The default path is the project root.

‘write_file’
     Create or replace a file with the given contents.  This is an edit.

‘replace’
     Replace one unique string in a file.  If the string occurs more
     than once, the call fails unless ‘replace_all’ is true.  This is an
     edit.

‘apply_patch’
     Apply several hunks in one call.  Each hunk names a ‘path’, an
     ‘old_string’, and a ‘new_string’.  The old string must occur once
     in that file.  Later hunks on the same file see earlier
     replacements.  If any hunk fails, no file is changed.  This is an
     edit.

     In plan mode, ‘write_file’, ‘replace’, ‘apply_patch’, and
     ‘notebook_edit’ fail.  The model must write ‘plan.md’ with
     ‘write_plan’.  *Note Plan mode::.


