10.13 Computer use
==================

Harmless can see the screen, click, type, and open a browser the user
can watch.

   ‘computer_screenshot’ returns the width, the height, and a PNG path
under the Harmless data directory, in ‘computer/’.  The file is not in
the project.

   ‘computer_click’ clicks at ‘x’ and ‘y’.  A missing ‘button’ is left.
Nil and a value that is not an integer are refused: ‘x must be an
integer’ or ‘y must be an integer’.  A negative integer is refused: ‘x
must be a non-negative integer’.  A button other than left, right, or
middle is refused: ‘button must be left, right, or middle’.

   ‘computer_type’ types ‘text’ into the focused window.  Nil and a
value that is not text are refused: ‘text must be a string’.  ‘""’  and
whitespace are refused: ‘text is empty’.  ‘/’ and ‘c:/’ are characters
to type.

   ‘computer_key’ presses one key, such as enter, tab, escape, a
function key from f1 to f12, or one character.  Nil, ‘""’, and
whitespace are refused: ‘key is empty’.  A value that is not text is
refused: ‘key must be a string’.  Anything else, including ‘c:/’, is
refused: ‘key is not a key’.  ‘/’ is a key.

   ‘browser_open’ opens ‘url’ in the desktop browser.  Nil, ‘""’, and
whitespace are refused: ‘url is empty’.  A value that is not text is
refused: ‘url must be a string’.  ‘/’ and ‘c:/’ are refused: ‘url must
be http or https’.

   The class is ‘shell’.  The tools ask in ‘ask’ mode and in
‘accept-edits’.  ‘always-approve’ does not ask.  In plan mode a click,
typed text, a key, and the browser are refused before the question:
‘Error: Plan mode is on. Computer control is refused’.  A screenshot
still runs.  A read-only subagent is not offered these tools.  A
detached chat is offered them.  Nothing is written into the project.


File: harmless.info,  Node: Monitors,  Next: Schedules,  Prev: Computer use,  Up: Tools

10.14 Monitors
==============

‘monitor’ watches one source until a line matches ‘pattern’.  The source
is a ‘path’ inside the project or an added directory, a ‘command’, or
the id of a background ‘shell’.  Pass one of those.  None is refused:
‘monitor source is missing’.  More than one is refused: ‘monitor source
must be one’.

   Nil and a value that is not text are refused: ‘pattern must be a
string’.  ‘""’  and whitespace are refused: ‘pattern is empty’.  A regex
Emacs cannot compile is refused: ‘pattern is not a pattern’.  ‘/’ and
‘c:/’ are patterns, not paths.

   A path is resolved inside the project or an added directory.  A value
that is not text is refused: ‘path must be a string’.  ‘""’  and
whitespace are refused: ‘Path is empty’.  ‘/’, ‘c:/’, and a path that
leaves the project and every added directory are refused: ‘Path escapes
project: ’, followed by the path.  A directory, including a trailing
slash, is refused: ‘monitor path is a directory’.  A missing file is
refused: ‘monitor file is missing’.  Lines already in the file do not
match.  Later lines do.

   A command uses the same read-only check as the shell.  A value that
is not text is refused: ‘command must be a string’.  ‘""’  and
whitespace are refused: ‘command is empty’.  A shell id that is not text
is refused: ‘shell id must be a string’.  A negative number is refused:
‘shell id is not an id’.  ‘""’  and whitespace are refused: ‘shell id is
empty’.  An unknown shell id is refused: ‘no background shell ’,
followed by the id.  ‘/’ and ‘c:/’ are ids, not paths.

   A match sends ‘Monitor ’, the id, ‘ matched:’, and the line.  The
session is idle, so that starts a turn.  A session that is already in a
turn queues the line and keeps going.  ‘monitor_stop’ stops the watch.
A command this monitor started is killed.  A background shell that was
only watched keeps running.  Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused:
‘monitor id is empty’.  A value that is not text is refused: ‘monitor id
must be a string’.  A negative number is refused: ‘monitor id is not an
id’.  An unknown id is refused: ‘no monitor ’, followed by the id.
Stopping a monitor that has already stopped is refused: ‘monitor ’, the
id, and ‘ is not running’.

   A file watch does not ask.  A read-only command does not ask.  A
command that can write asks in ‘ask’ mode and in ‘accept-edits’.
‘always-approve’ does not ask.  In plan mode that command is refused:
‘Error: Plan mode is on. A shell command that can write is refused’.  A
file watch and a read-only command still run.  A read-only subagent may
watch a file or a read-only command.  A detached chat is not offered
these tools.  Nothing is written into the project.  The watch is
forgotten when Emacs exits.


File: harmless.info,  Node: Schedules,  Next: Todos,  Prev: Monitors,  Up: Tools

10.15 Schedules
===============

‘schedule’ sends ‘prompt’ once, at a later time.  Pass ‘delay’ in
seconds, or ‘at’ as a UTC time such as ‘2099-01-01T00:00:00Z’.  Pass one
of those.  None is refused: ‘schedule time is missing’.  More than one
is refused: ‘schedule time must be one’.

   Nil and a value that is not text are refused: ‘prompt must be a
string’.  ‘""’  and whitespace are refused: ‘prompt is empty’.  ‘/’,
‘c:/’, ‘log.txt’, and ‘sub/’ are prompt text, not paths.  They are not
resolved, and they do not create a file or a directory.

   A delay that is not a positive number is refused: ‘delay must be a
positive number’.  Zero and a negative number are refused the same way.
A time that is not text is refused: ‘at must be a string’.  ‘""’  and
whitespace are refused: ‘at is empty’.  A value Emacs cannot parse,
including ‘/’ and ‘c:/’, is refused: ‘at is not a time’.  A time that
has already passed is refused: ‘schedule time has passed’.

   The prompt and the absolute time are saved with the session.  When
that session is loaded, a schedule that is still in the future is armed
again.  A schedule that has expired is removed and is not sent.  This is
one prompt, once.  It does not repeat, and it does not watch a queue or
a context wall.

   When the time arrives, the prompt is sent.  The session is idle, so
that starts a turn.  A session that is already in a turn queues the
prompt and keeps going.  ‘schedule_cancel’ removes a waiting prompt.
The prompt is not sent.  Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused:
‘schedule id is empty’.  A value that is not text is refused: ‘schedule
id must be a string’.  A negative number is refused: ‘schedule id is not
an id’.  An unknown id is refused: ‘no schedule ’, followed by the id.
‘/’ and ‘c:/’ are ids, not paths.

   The class is ‘edit’.  The tools ask in ‘ask’ mode, and the question
shows the prompt, or the id when cancelling.  ‘accept-edits’ and
‘always-approve’ do not ask.  Plan mode does not refuse scheduling.  The
turn that runs later still obeys plan mode.  A read-only subagent is not
offered these tools.  A workspace subagent may schedule.  A detached
chat is offered them.  Nothing is written into the project.  Forking a
session does not copy its schedules.


File: harmless.info,  Node: Todos,  Next: Review,  Prev: Schedules,  Up: Tools

10.16 Todos
===========

‘todo_write’ keeps a list of work on the session.  Each item has an id,
content, a status, and the ids it depends on.  Status is ‘pending’,
‘in_progress’, ‘completed’, or ‘cancelled’.  A missing status on a new
item is ‘pending’.

   ‘merge’ true, or omitted, updates items by id and appends an id that
is new.  A field that is omitted stays as it was.  ‘merge’ false
replaces the whole list.  JSON null and ‘[]’ are an empty list.  A
missing ‘todos’ value is refused: ‘todos must be a list’.  A value that
is not a list is refused the same way.  A merge value that is not a
boolean is refused: ‘todo merge must be a boolean’.

   An item that is not an item is refused: ‘todo must be an item’.  Nil,
‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘todo id is empty’.  A value that is
not text is refused: ‘todo id must be a string’.  The same empty and
non-text refusals apply to content: ‘todo content is empty’ and ‘todo
content must be a string’.  A new item needs content.  An update can
omit it.  A status outside the four names is refused: ‘todo status is
not a status’.  An id repeated in one call is refused: ‘todo id is
duplicate’.

   ‘depends’ lists ids.  Omitted, it stays as it was on an update and is
empty on a new item.  JSON null and ‘[]’ clear it.  A value that is not
a list is refused: ‘todo depends must be a list’.  An entry that is not
text is refused: ‘todo depends must be a string’.  An empty entry is
refused: ‘todo depends is empty’.  A repeated entry is refused: ‘todo
depends is duplicate’.  An item that depends on its own id is refused:
‘todo depends on itself’.  An unknown id is refused: ‘todo depends is
missing’.  A cycle is refused: ‘todo depends is a cycle’.  A dependency
does not block a status change.  The list shows it.

   ‘/’, ‘c:/’, ‘notes’, and ‘sub/’ are text, not paths.  They are not
resolved, and they do not create a file or a directory.  The list is
saved with the session.  A fork copies it.  A subagent starts with an
empty list.  Loading a session keeps the list.  A saved item that is not
usable is dropped.  A dependency that is missing, repeated, on itself,
or that closes a cycle is dropped.  The class is ‘read’, so the tool
does not ask.  Plan mode does not refuse it.  A read-only subagent may
update its own list.  A detached chat is offered the tool.  Nothing is
written into the project.  The session header shows how many items are
pending or in progress.


File: harmless.info,  Node: Review,  Next: Language server,  Prev: Todos,  Up: Tools

10.17 Review
============

‘M-x harmless-review’ reads the working tree, a base branch, or one
commit.  The menu key is ‘R’.  The model uses the same choice through
‘review’.  Omit ‘base’ and ‘commit’ to read the working tree.  ‘base’ is
a branch name, and the diff is that branch compared with ‘HEAD’.
‘commit’ is one commit, such as ‘HEAD’ or a hash.  Passing both is
refused: ‘review has both a base and a commit’.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘review base is empty’ or
‘review commit is empty’.  A value that is not text is refused: ‘review
base must be a string’ or ‘review commit must be a string’.  ‘/’, ‘c:/’,
a drive root, ‘~’, ‘..’, a leading dash, and any other absolute path are
refused and are not resolved: ‘review base is not a branch’ or ‘review
commit is not a commit’.  A name git does not know is refused the same
way.  A range is not one commit.

   ‘findings’ records the result.  Omit it and the tool returns the
diff, cut at ‘harmless-review-max-bytes’ (100000).  A cut diff ends with
‘[truncated]’.  The stored review is left unchanged.  JSON null and ‘[]’
record an empty list, and the result is ‘No findings’.  A missing list
is refused: ‘review findings must be a list’.  A value that is not a
list is refused the same way.  An entry that is not a finding is
refused: ‘review finding must be an item’.

   Each finding has a severity, text, and an optional file and line.
Severity is ‘high’, ‘medium’, or ‘low’.  Anything else is refused:
‘review severity is not a severity’.  Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are
refused: ‘review finding is empty’.  A value that is not text is
refused: ‘review finding must be a string’.  A file that is present and
empty is refused: ‘review file is empty’.  A file that is not text is
refused: ‘review file must be a string’.  A line that is present and is
not a positive integer is refused: ‘review line is not a line’.  ‘/’,
‘c:/’, ‘notes’, and ‘sub/’ are text, not paths.  They are not resolved,
and they do not create a file or a directory.

   The list replaces the previous review.  It is saved with the session.
A fork copies it.  A subagent starts without one.  Loading a session
keeps the review.  A saved review that is not usable is dropped.  A
saved finding that is not usable is dropped.  The class is ‘read’, so
the tool does not ask.  Plan mode does not refuse it.  A read-only
subagent may review the project.  A detached chat is not offered the
tool.  Git is used only to read.  Nothing is written into the project,
and a finding is not applied as an edit.

   A project that is not a git repository is refused: ‘this project is
not a git repository’.  A missing directory is not created.  Nil, ‘""’,
a relative path, ‘~’, ‘/’, and a drive root are refused: ‘This chat is
not attached to a project’.  They are not resolved.  When git cannot be
found: ‘git is not available’.  When a diff cannot be read: ‘review
could not read the diff’.

   ‘harmless-review-function’, when set, is called by ‘M-x
harmless-review’ as ‘(session args diff)’.  A list of findings is
recorded.  Nil leaves the stored review unchanged and the command
returns the diff.  The tool does not call it.  It must not start a turn,
and it must not edit the project.  The session header shows how many
findings are recorded.


File: harmless.info,  Node: Language server,  Prev: Review,  Up: Tools

10.18 Language server
=====================

‘lsp’ asks a language server that is already running in Emacs.  The
operation is ‘definition’, ‘references’, or ‘diagnostics’.  ‘M-x
harmless-lsp’ asks the same way.  The menu key is ‘L’.

   ‘path’ is a file in the project, or in a directory added for this
session.  A definition or a list of references also takes ‘line’ and
‘column’.  Both start at 1.  Diagnostics read the whole file and take no
position.  The file must already be open in a buffer whose server is
running.  Harmless does not start a server, and it does not open the
file to find one.

   A definition or a reference is one line, ‘FILE:LINE:COLUMN’.  The
column in that line starts at 1.  No location is ‘No definition’ or ‘No
references’.  A diagnostic is ‘LINE:COLUMN: SEVERITY: TEXT’.  Severity
is ‘error’, ‘warning’, or ‘note’.  No diagnostic is ‘No diagnostics’.
Text that spans lines is folded onto one line.

   The class is ‘read’, so the tool does not ask.  Plan mode does not
refuse it.  A read-only subagent may call it.  A detached chat is not
offered the tool.  Nothing is written into the project.  ‘write_file’
still reports only the path and the byte count.  Diagnostics are a later
‘lsp’ call.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace for the operation are refused: ‘lsp
operation is empty’.  A value that is not text is refused: ‘lsp
operation must be a string’.  Any other name is refused: ‘lsp operation
is not an operation’.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace for the path are refused: ‘lsp path is
empty’.  A value that is not text is refused: ‘lsp path must be a
string’.  ‘/’, ‘c:/’, and a drive root are refused and are not expanded:
‘lsp path is the filesystem root’.  A missing file, a directory, and a
trailing slash are refused: ‘lsp path is not a file’.  A path outside
the project and outside every added directory is refused: ‘Path escapes
project: ’, followed by the path.  A detached chat with a relative path
is refused: ‘This chat is not attached to a project’.

   A missing line is refused: ‘lsp line is empty’.  A missing column is
refused: ‘lsp column is empty’.  Zero, a negative number, and a value
that is not an integer are refused: ‘lsp line is not a line’ or ‘lsp
column is not a column’.  A position on diagnostics is refused: ‘lsp
diagnostics takes no position’.

   When no buffer is visiting the file, or that buffer has no server:
‘lsp server is not running’.  A failed request is refused: ‘lsp query
failed’.

   ‘harmless-lsp-query-function’, when set, is called instead of the
server as ‘(session op path line column)’.  ‘op’ is ‘definition’,
‘references’, or ‘diagnostics’.  ‘path’ is absolute.  ‘line’ and
‘column’ are nil for diagnostics.  It returns the text the model sees.
Nil is refused: ‘lsp query returned nothing’.  A value that is not text
is refused: ‘lsp query must be a string’.  It must not start a turn, and
it must not edit the project.


