13 Plugins
**********

A plugin is one directory.  It can hold skills, agents, a ‘hooks.json’
file, and an ‘mcp.json’ file.  ‘M-x harmless-plugin-install’ copies that
directory as one unit.  It does not merge those files into
‘.harmless/skills’, ‘.harmless/agents’, or the project's ‘mcp.json’.
‘M-x harmless-plugin-inspect’ reads one plugin directory.  It lists the
skill ids whose ‘SKILL.md’ has a usable summary, the hooks, and the MCP
server names in file order.  It writes nothing and it does not copy the
plugin.  Installing stays the explicit copy above.

   Nil, ‘""’, whitespace, and a value that is not text are refused:
‘plugin directory is empty’.  A relative path, including ‘~’, is refused
and is not expanded: ‘plugin directory must be absolute’.  ‘/’ and a
drive root are refused: ‘plugin directory is the filesystem root’.  A
missing plugin directory is refused: ‘plugin directory is missing’.  A
file is refused: ‘plugin directory is not a directory’.  A missing or
unreadable ‘plugin.json’ is refused: ‘plugin.json is not valid’.

   The copy for a project is ‘.harmless/plugins/NAME’.  The copy for the
user is ‘plugins/NAME’ under the Harmless data directory.  A later
plugin name wins when two installed plugins define the same skill,
agent, or MCP server.  A project copy wins over a user copy.  Deleting
the copied directory removes the bundle.

   A marketplace is a directory.  When it contains ‘marketplace.json’,
that file is the list of plugins.  ‘source’ is a relative path inside
the marketplace.  An absolute path, ‘~’, and a path that leaves the
marketplace are refused.  With no ‘marketplace.json’, each child
directory whose ‘plugin.json’ name matches the directory is a plugin.

   ‘plugin.json’ names the plugin.  The name is a plugin id, not a path.
Skills live in ‘skills/ID/SKILL.md’.  Agents live in ‘agents/NAME.md’.
‘hooks.json’ is a list of hooks.  ‘mcp.json’ uses the same ‘mcpServers’
object as the project file.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘plugin name is empty’.  A
value that is not text is refused: ‘plugin name must be a string’.  A
path, ‘~’, and the filesystem root are refused: ‘plugin name is not a
name’.  A missing plugin is refused: ‘no plugin named ’, followed by the
id.  A relative marketplace, including ‘~’, is refused and is not
expanded: ‘plugin directory must be absolute’.  ‘/’ and a drive root are
refused: ‘plugin directory is the filesystem root’.  A detached chat has
no project copy: ‘This chat is not attached to a project’.  A second
copy is refused: ‘plugin is already installed: ’, followed by the id.


