15 Image generation
*******************

‘generate_image’ writes an image into the project.  The model passes
‘prompt’ and ‘path’.  A relative path is resolved against the session
directory.  It is not resolved against the buffer's default directory.
‘~’ is not expanded.

   The bytes come from ‘harmless-image-generate-function’.  When that
variable is nil, the tool is refused: ‘image generation is not
configured’.  The function is not called until the prompt and the path
are accepted.  Plan mode does not call it: ‘Plan mode is on. Only
plan.md may be edited, with write_plan’.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘image prompt is empty’.  A
value that is not text is refused: ‘image prompt must be a string’.  A
missing or blank path is refused: ‘image path is empty’.  A path that is
not text is refused: ‘image path must be a string’.  A path that names a
directory is refused: ‘image path is not a file’.  ‘~’ is refused:
‘image path must be absolute’.  A path outside the project is refused:
‘image path escapes the project: ’, followed by the path.  Bytes that
are not an image are refused: ‘image is not an image’.  Nothing is
written in that case.

   A detached chat and a blank project directory are refused: ‘This chat
is not attached to a project’.  A relative project directory is refused
and is not expanded: ‘image directory must be absolute’.  ‘/’ and a
drive root are refused: ‘image directory is the filesystem root’.  ‘/’
as a path is refused: ‘image path is the filesystem root’.

   The tool is an edit.  A detached chat is not offered it.  A
successful call reports the absolute path and the number of bytes
written.


