17 Pages
********

‘M-x harmless-publish’ writes one HTML page from a Markdown or HTML file
in the project.  The source file is not modified.

   Nil PATH writes ‘.harmless/pages/NAME.html’, where NAME is the source
file's name without its extension.  A relative destination stays inside
the project.  An absolute destination is written only when its parent
already exists.  ‘~’ is not expanded.

   Markdown becomes a document.  A heading line is ‘#’ through ‘######’
followed by a space.  A blank line separates paragraphs.  A fenced block
is three backticks.  Inline code is one backtick span.  A link is
‘[label](target)’.  Those parts are rendered.  The other text is
escaped, so a ‘<script>’ in the Markdown is text.

   An HTML file that already contains a document is copied.  A fragment
is wrapped in a document.  Publishing again overwrites the page.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘page directory is empty’.  A
directory that is not text is refused: ‘page directory must be a
string’.  A relative project directory, including ‘~’, is refused and is
not expanded: ‘page directory must be absolute’.  ‘/’ and a drive root
are refused: ‘page directory is the filesystem root’.  A missing project
directory is refused: ‘page directory is missing’.  A file is refused:
‘page directory is not a directory’.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘page source is empty’.  A
source that is not text is refused: ‘page source must be a string’.  ‘/’
and a drive root are refused: ‘page source is the filesystem root’.  ‘~’
is refused and is not expanded: ‘page source must be absolute’.  A
relative source that leaves the project is refused: ‘page source escapes
the project: ’, followed by the path.  A missing source is refused:
‘page source is missing’.  A directory is refused: ‘page source is not a
file’.  A file that is not Markdown or HTML is refused: ‘page source is
not a page’.

   Nil is the default destination.  ‘""’  and whitespace are refused:
‘page path is empty’.  A path that is not text is refused: ‘page path
must be a string’.  ‘/’ and a drive root are refused: ‘page path is the
filesystem root’.  ‘~’ is refused: ‘page path must be absolute’.  A
trailing slash is refused: ‘page path is not a file’.  A relative path
that leaves the project is refused: ‘page path escapes the project: ’,
followed by the path.  A destination that is not ‘.html’ or ‘.htm’ is
refused: ‘page path is not a page’.  An absolute destination whose
parent is missing is refused: ‘page path is missing’.  The source file
as the destination is refused: ‘page path is the source’.


