file.  ‘M-x harmless-team-image-start’ records another seat from that
file.  The new seat copies the role and the inbound work, and it starts
with no session.  The source seat stays.  ‘M-x harmless-team-packet’
captures what that seat knows: the recap, or the inbound work when there
is no recap.  ‘M-x harmless-team-packet-apply’ puts that work back on
the same seat and binds a session that is already running.  The runtime
must change.  The seat keeps its name.  Nothing is started.  A blank
image name is refused: ‘team image is empty’.  A name that is not text
is refused: ‘team image must be a string’.  Any other name is refused:
‘team image is not a name’.  An image that already exists is refused:
‘team image already exists’.  A missing image is refused: ‘team image is
missing’.  An image file that cannot be read is refused: ‘team image is
not valid’.  An empty seat is refused: ‘team seat is not occupied’.  A
seat that is already recorded is refused: ‘team seat already exists’.  A
blank packet name is refused: ‘team packet is empty’.  A name that is
not text is refused: ‘team packet must be a string’.  Any other name is
refused: ‘team packet is not a name’.  A packet that already exists is
refused: ‘team packet already exists’.  A missing packet is refused:
‘team packet is missing’.  A packet file that cannot be read is refused:
‘team packet is not valid’.  A seat that knows nothing is refused: ‘team
packet is empty’.  The same runtime is refused: ‘team packet is the same
runtime’.

   ‘M-x harmless-team-compact-plan’ lists Harmless seats at or above a
percent of the context window.  It does not write, and it does not
compact.  ‘M-x harmless-team-compact’ records why that seat is compacted
and tells the room, on the topic ‘compact’.  The seat must already be at
that wall.  ‘M-x harmless-team-compacts’ reads those notices, oldest
first.  The transcript summary is ‘M-x harmless-compact’.  Nothing is
started.  A blank percent is refused: ‘team compact percent is empty’.
Any other percent is refused: ‘team compact percent is not a percent’.
A blank reason is refused: ‘team compact why is empty’.  A reason that
is not text is refused: ‘team compact why must be a string’.  An empty
seat is refused: ‘team seat is not occupied’.  A seat below the wall is
refused: ‘team seat is not near the wall’.

   A blank runtime is refused: ‘team runtime is empty’.  A runtime that
is not text is refused: ‘team runtime must be a string’.  Any other
runtime is refused: ‘team runtime is not a runtime’.  A blank session is
refused: ‘team session is empty’.  A session that is not text is
refused: ‘team session must be a string’.  A Harmless id that is not a
session id is refused: ‘team session is not an id’.  A missing session
is refused: ‘team session is missing’.  Two Harmless directories with
the same id are refused: ‘team session is not one session’.  ‘/’ and a
drive root are refused: ‘team session is the filesystem root’.  ‘~’ and
a relative path are refused and are not expanded: ‘team session must be
absolute’.  A terminal process that is not running is refused: ‘team
session is not running’.  Releasing an empty seat is refused: ‘team seat
is not occupied’.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘team edge is empty’.  An edge
that is not text is refused: ‘team edge must be a string’.  Any other
kind is refused: ‘team edge is not a kind’.  An end that is not a seat
reference is refused: ‘team edge is not a seat’.  An edge from a seat to
itself is refused: ‘team edge is the same seat’.  The same edge again is
refused: ‘team edge already exists’.  An edge that would loop the launch
order is refused: ‘team edge is a cycle’.  The rig file is left
unchanged.

   A blank spec is refused: ‘team spec is empty’.  A spec that is not
text is refused: ‘team spec must be a string’.  ‘/’ and a drive root are
refused: ‘team spec is the filesystem root’.  ‘~’ and a relative path
are refused and are not expanded: ‘team spec must be absolute’.  A
missing file, or a directory with no ‘rig.json’, is refused: ‘team spec
is missing’.  A broken spec is refused: ‘team spec is not valid’.  The
spec file is left unchanged.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘team rig is empty’.  A rig
that is not text is refused: ‘team rig must be a string’.  A path is
refused: ‘team rig is not a name’.  A pod and a seat use the same three
sentences, with ‘pod’ or ‘seat’ in place of ‘rig’.  A role uses the
empty and must-be-a-string sentences.  A session uses them too, and an
id that is not a session id is refused: ‘team session is not an id’.
Work text uses the empty and must-be-a-string sentences.

   A second seat with the same name is refused: ‘team seat already
exists’.  A missing rig is refused: ‘team rig is missing’.  A missing
seat is refused: ‘team seat is missing’.  A broken rig file is refused:
‘team rig is not valid’.  That file is left unchanged.

   A team file is refused at the filesystem root: ‘Refusing to store a
team at ’, followed by that directory.

   ‘team_boot’ calls ‘M-x harmless-team-boot’.  ‘team_inspect’ reads the
seats, the edges, the launch order, and the rows.  It writes nothing.
‘team_message’ calls ‘M-x harmless-team-send’.  The seat must already be
occupied.  ‘team_snapshot’ calls ‘M-x harmless-team-snapshot’.  The live
rig is not changed.  ‘team_restore’ calls ‘M-x
harmless-team-snapshot-restore’.  A seat that cannot return writes
nothing.

   A detached chat is not offered these tools.  Calling one there is
refused: ‘This chat is not attached to a project’.  A missing session is
refused: ‘No Harmless session’.  Plan mode refuses the tools that write:
‘Plan mode is on. Only plan.md may be edited, with write_plan’.  Inspect
still reads.  The command errors are unchanged, including ‘team spec is
empty’, ‘team rig is missing’, ‘team send is empty’, ‘team seat is not
occupied’, ‘team snapshot is missing’, and ‘team snapshot cannot
restore’.

   A seat can name an auth profile for its runtime.  *Note Profiles::.
Switching that profile keeps the session and the inbound work.  The rig
stores the profile name and never the token.


