19 Machines
***********

A machine is a name and a directory.  The directory is that host's
Harmless data.  ‘M-x harmless-machine-add’ records both.  It does not
open a connection, start a process, or store a secret.  ‘M-x
harmless-machine-list’ returns the names.  ‘M-x harmless-machine-show’
returns the name and the directory.  ‘M-x harmless-machine-remove’
forgets the name and leaves the directory on disk.

   The registry is ‘machines.json’ under the local Harmless data
directory.  A missing file is an empty registry.

   ‘M-x harmless-machine-call’ runs one public team command with that
host's directory as ‘harmless-directory’.  The verb is a command whose
name starts with ‘harmless-team-’.  A private helper is refused.  An
interactive call prompts for the verb's own arguments.  The registry
stays on this machine.

   ‘M-x harmless-machine-copy’ copies one relative file from one host
directory to another.  A directory is refused.  A file that is already
at the destination is refused.  ‘..’, ‘~’, and an absolute path are
refused and are not opened.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘machine name is empty’.  A
value that is not text is refused: ‘machine name must be a string’.  A
path, ‘~’, and the filesystem root are refused: ‘machine name is not a
name’.  A second registration is refused: ‘machine is already
registered: ’, followed by the name.  A missing machine is refused: ‘no
machine named ’, followed by the name.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘machine directory is empty’.
A value that is not text is refused: ‘machine directory must be a
string’.  A relative path, including ‘~’, is refused and is not
expanded: ‘machine directory must be absolute’.  ‘/’ and a drive root
are refused: ‘machine directory is the filesystem root’.  A missing
directory is refused: ‘machine directory is missing’.  A file is
refused: ‘machine directory is not a directory’.  A trailing slash names
the same directory.

   A verb that is not a public team command is refused: ‘machine verb is
not a team verb’.  A broken registry is refused: ‘machines are not
valid’.  That file is left unchanged.  The registry is refused at the
filesystem root: ‘Refusing to store a machine at ’, followed by that
directory.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘machine file is empty’.  A
value that is not text is refused: ‘machine file must be a string’.  A
path that leaves the host is refused: ‘machine file escapes the
machine’.  A missing file is refused: ‘machine file is missing’.  A
directory is refused: ‘machine file is not a file’.  An existing
destination is refused: ‘machine file is already there’.


