20 People
*********

A person is an address, ‘name@slack’.  Asking that person opens a queue
row.  The row's history is the receipt.  Slack is the connector.  ‘M-x
harmless-person-add’ records the name and the channel.  A leading ‘#’ on
the channel is not stored.  The Slack token is not stored.

   ‘M-x harmless-person-list’ returns the names.  A missing file is an
empty list and writes nothing.  ‘M-x harmless-person-show’ returns one
person.  ‘M-x harmless-person-remove’ forgets the name.  Rows already
opened for that address stay.

   ‘M-x harmless-person-ask’ opens a row whose seat is the address and
whose body is the question.  The history records that the team asked,
then whether Slack was posted.  The token is read from the environment
variable ‘SLACK_BOT_TOKEN’ only when a sender is set.  With no sender,
the receipt says the message was not posted.  Nothing is started, and no
connection is opened.

   The people file is ‘RIG.people.json’ beside the rig file.  It is not
part of the rig.  A missing rig is refused: ‘team rig is missing’.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘person name is empty’.  A
value that is not text is refused: ‘person name must be a string’.  A
path, ‘~’, a hyphen, and the filesystem root are refused: ‘person name
is not a name’.  A second registration is refused: ‘person is already
registered: ’, followed by the name.  A missing person is refused: ‘no
person named ’, followed by the name.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘person channel is empty’.  A
value that is not text is refused: ‘person channel must be a string’.  A
path, ‘~’, a space, and a token are refused: ‘person channel is not a
channel’.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘person question is empty’.  A
value that is not text is refused: ‘person question must be a string’.

   A broken people file is refused: ‘people are not valid’.  That file
is left unchanged.  A token, a secret, or a password in that file is
refused the same way.  The people file is refused at the filesystem
root: ‘Refusing to store a person at ’, followed by that directory.


