21 Profiles
***********

A profile is a name and a runtime.  The third field is the name of an
environment variable.  The token is that variable's value.  ‘M-x
harmless-profile-add’ records those three.  It does not store the token.
‘M-x harmless-profile-list’ returns the names.  A missing file is an
empty list and writes nothing.  ‘M-x harmless-profile-show’ returns one
profile and whether its variable is set.  The token is not in that
result.  ‘M-x harmless-profile-remove’ forgets the name.  A seat that
already names it keeps that name, its session, and its inbound work.

   ‘M-x harmless-profile-switch’ points an occupied seat at one profile.
The profile's runtime must already be the seat's runtime.  The session
and the inbound work stay.  The rig stores the profile name and never
the token.  This is not ‘M-x harmless-login’.  Nothing is started, and
no connection is opened.

   The profile file is ‘profiles.json’ under the local Harmless data
directory.  It is not part of the rig.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘profile name is empty’.  A
value that is not text is refused: ‘profile name must be a string’.  A
path, ‘~’, a hyphen, and the filesystem root are refused: ‘profile name
is not a name’.  A second registration is refused: ‘profile is already
registered: ’, followed by the name.  A missing profile is refused: ‘no
profile named ’, followed by the name.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘profile runtime is empty’.  A
value that is not text is refused: ‘profile runtime must be a string’.
Any other runtime is refused: ‘profile runtime is not a runtime’.  The
runtimes are ‘harmless’, ‘claude’, ‘codex’, ‘pi’, and ‘terminal’.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘profile env is empty’.  A
value that is not text is refused: ‘profile env must be a string’.  A
path, ‘~’, a lowercase name, and a token are refused: ‘profile env is
not a name’.

   An empty seat is refused: ‘team seat is not occupied’.  A profile for
a different runtime is refused: ‘profile runtime does not match’.  The
seat is left unchanged.

   A broken profile file is refused: ‘profiles are not valid’.  That
file is left unchanged.  A token, a secret, or a password in that file
is refused the same way.  A token key in the rig is refused: ‘team rig
is not valid’.  That file is left unchanged.  The profile file is
refused at the filesystem root: ‘Refusing to store a profile at ’,
followed by that directory.


