24 Scope
********

A project directory holds missions, and a mission holds slices.  ‘M-x
harmless-scope-project’ writes ‘SPEC.md’ in the project.  ‘M-x
harmless-scope-mission’ writes ‘missions/NAME/SPEC.md’.  ‘M-x
harmless-scope-slice’ writes ‘missions/NAME/slices/NAME/SPEC.md’.  Each
file starts with ‘# Intent’.  Only a slice also has ‘# Specification’.
‘M-x harmless-scope-show’ composes the project intent, the mission
intent, and the slice intent.  Show writes nothing.

   The specification is one item per non-blank line.  ‘M-x
harmless-scope-proof’ stores evidence as ‘proof/NAME.md’ under the
slice.  ‘M-x harmless-scope-judge’ appends one attributed ‘accept’,
‘reject’, or ‘withdraw’ to ‘judgments.json’.  The judgment names the
judge, the reason, and the proof name.  ‘M-x harmless-scope-progress’
derives ‘proved’, ‘rejected’, or ‘open’ from the latest judgment whose
proof file is still in the slice.  The slice is ‘proved’ only when it
has an item and each latest verdict is ‘accept’.  One latest ‘reject’ is
‘rejected’.  Anything else, including ‘withdraw’, is ‘open’.  Progress
writes nothing.  Nothing is started.

   A name is letters and digits.  ‘/’ is valid intent, specification,
proof text, judge, and reason, and it is not opened as a path.  A
relative project, including ‘~’, is refused and is not expanded.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘scope project is empty’.  A
project that is not text is refused: ‘scope project must be a string’.
‘/’ and a drive root are refused: ‘scope project is the filesystem
root’.  A relative project is refused: ‘scope project must be absolute’.
A missing project is refused: ‘scope project is missing’.  A file is
refused: ‘scope project is not a directory’.  A second project intent is
refused: ‘scope project already exists’.  The project directory is not
created.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘scope intent is empty’.
Intent that is not text is refused: ‘scope intent must be a string’.  A
specification uses the same two sentences, with ‘spec’ in place of
‘intent’.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘scope mission is empty’.  A
mission that is not text is refused: ‘scope mission must be a string’.
Any other mission is refused: ‘scope mission is not a name’.  A missing
mission is refused: ‘scope mission is missing’.  A second mission is
refused: ‘scope mission already exists’.  A project with no intent is
refused: ‘scope project has no intent’.  A slice, a proof, and an
evidence name use the same three sentences, with ‘slice’, ‘proof’, or
‘evidence’ in place of ‘mission’.  A missing slice is refused: ‘scope
slice is missing’.  A second slice is refused: ‘scope slice already
exists’.  A second proof is refused: ‘scope proof already exists’.  A
missing proof is refused: ‘scope evidence is missing’.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘scope item is empty’.  Zero,
a past-the-end number, and any other item are refused: ‘scope item is
not an item’.  Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘scope verdict is
empty’.  A verdict that is not text is refused: ‘scope verdict must be a
string’.  Any other verdict is refused: ‘scope verdict is not a
verdict’.  A judge and a reason use the empty and must-be-a-string
sentences, with ‘judge’ or ‘reason’ in place of ‘verdict’.

   A slice with no specification is refused: ‘scope slice is not
specified’.  A file that is not intent is refused: ‘scope file is not
valid’.  A judgment file that cannot be read is refused: ‘scope
judgments are not valid’.  That file is left unchanged.  A scope path at
the filesystem root is refused: ‘Refusing to store scope at ’, followed
by that path.


