26 Memory
*********

Memory is Markdown under ‘harmless-directory’, in ‘memory’.  Global
notes apply to every project.  Workspace notes belong to one project.  A
detached chat has workspace memory unavailable and global memory
available.

   Each scope has three directories:

‘topics’
     Curated notes, one file per topic.

‘observations/_inbox’
     New facts, not yet folded into a topic.

‘archive’
     Inbox files that ‘harmless-dream’ has folded.

   ‘MEMORY.md’ in each scope is a generated index.  A turn receives the
index, not the notes.

‘M-x harmless-remember’
     Save a title and a note in workspace memory.  A prefix argument
     saves it in global memory.

‘M-x harmless-dream’
     Fold the inbox into topics for this project and for global memory.
     The inbox files move to ‘archive’.

   The model uses three tools.

‘memory_read’
     Read one memory file.  ‘scope’ is ‘workspace’ or ‘global’.

‘memory_remember’
     Append a fact to the inbox.  ‘topic’ is an optional slug, such as
     ‘emacs’.

‘memory_write_topic’
     Replace one topic file with the full Markdown you supply.

   A finished turn can write one inbox observation.  Set
‘harmless-memory-observe-function’ to a function of the session.  It
returns a plist with ‘:title’ and ‘:body’, and optional ‘:topic’ and
‘:scope’.  Nil writes nothing.  The function is not called when the turn
aborts or the reply is empty.  A tool call does not write one until the
turn is idle.  The transcript is not modified.  An unset function writes
nothing.

   A detached chat records a global observation.  An attached project
records a workspace observation.  ‘scope’ may name ‘workspace’ or
‘global’.

   Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace for the title or the body write nothing.  A
value that is not text is refused: ‘memory title must be a string’,
‘memory body must be a string’, or ‘memory topic must be a string’.  A
scope that is not a scope is refused: ‘memory scope is not a scope’.  A
scope that is not text is refused: ‘memory scope must be a string’.  A
relative project directory, including ‘~’, is refused and is not
expanded: ‘memory directory must be absolute’.  ‘/’ and a drive root are
refused: ‘memory directory is the filesystem root’.  A blank project
directory is refused: ‘This chat is not attached to a project’.  Not a
session is refused: ‘No Harmless session’.


