27 Plan mode
************

‘M-x harmless-plan’ turns plan mode on for the current session.  A
prefix argument turns it off.  The menu key is ‘P’.  The model may also
call ‘enter_plan_mode’, which asks you before it switches.

   While plan mode is on, the model is told to explore with read-only
tools, to write the plan only with ‘write_plan’, and to call
‘exit_plan_mode’ when the plan is ready.  ‘write_file’, ‘replace’,
‘apply_patch’, ‘notebook_edit’, and ‘generate_image’ fail.  A shell
command that can write is refused before any permission question:
‘Error: Plan mode is on. A shell command that can write is refused’.  A
read-only shell command still runs.  ‘shell_kill’ still asks.  A click,
typed text, a key, and a browser are refused: ‘Error: Plan mode is on.
Computer control is refused’.  A screenshot still runs.  *Note Computer
use::.  A file watch and a read-only command still run.  A command that
can write is refused.  *Note Monitors::.  Scheduling a prompt still
runs.  The later turn obeys plan mode.  *Note Schedules::.  A review
still runs, and it does not edit the project.  *Note Review::.  A
language server query still runs, and it does not edit the project.
*Note Language server::.  The header line shows ‘plan’.  ‘ask_user’ can
still ask a question.  *Note Questions::.

   ‘write_plan’ writes ‘plan.md’ in the session directory.  The contents
replace the whole file.  An empty plan is refused.

   ‘exit_plan_mode’ shows the plan and asks:

     Plan: a approve and build, c comment, s request changes, q quit

‘a’
     Turn plan mode off and tell the model to implement the plan.

‘c’
     Comment on the line at point.  An active region comments on that
     range of lines.  Nil, ‘""’, and whitespace are refused: ‘plan
     comment is empty’.  A value that is not text is refused: ‘plan
     comment must be a string’.  A missing line, a line past the end,
     and a value that is not a positive integer are refused: ‘plan
     comment line is not a line’.  A range whose end comes before its
     start is refused: ‘plan comment range is backwards’.  ‘/’ and ‘c:/’
     are comments, not paths.  A comment does not change ‘plan.md’.

‘s’
     Ask for revision notes, leave plan mode on, and send those notes
     back.  Comments already entered are included.  One line is sent as
     ‘Line N: TEXT’.  A range is sent as ‘Lines N-M: TEXT’.

‘q’
     Turn plan mode off and tell the model to stop without changing
     project files.

   Approving does not apply a patch by itself.  The same turn continues,
and later tool calls do the edits.

   A read-only shell command still runs.  A command that can write is
refused, including when the permission mode is ‘always-approve’.  *Note
Shell::.

   The flag is saved with the session.


File: harmless.info,  Node: Usage,  Next: Files,  Prev: Plan mode,  Up: Top

28 Usage
********

‘M-x harmless-usage’ shows two blocks.

   The session block is the context window of the current model, the
prompt size of the last request, and what remains in the window.  It
then shows the running prompt and completion totals for this chat.
Window sizes that Harmless does not learn from the provider live in
‘harmless-usage-context-windows’.  A model with no known window is
marked unknown.  Before the next prompt, Harmless compacts the
transcript when that prompt size has reached
‘harmless-compact-threshold’ percent of the window.  *Note Transcript::.

   The account block is the last rate-limit remainder each provider
sent.  A connection with no such headers says so.  For the connection
named ‘xAI’, the buffer also asks xAI for the current allowance when you
are not in batch Emacs.  This report is not an account credit balance.

   In the usage buffer, ‘g’ redraws and ‘q’ quits.


