29 Files
********

Harmless keeps its own files under ‘harmless-directory’.  The default is
‘harmless/’ in ‘user-emacs-directory’.  Nil and the empty string mean
that same default.  A relative path is refused.  The filesystem root is
refused.  A missing directory is created when it is needed.  It is not
replaced with ‘/’.

‘config.el’
     Optional configuration, loaded once.

‘auth.json’
‘auth-openai.json’
‘auth-anthropic.json’
‘auth-SLUG.json’
     OAuth tokens for each connection.  Harmless asks for mode 0600.  On
     Windows the file stays in the user profile; that filesystem does
     not store those mode bits.

‘profiles.json’
     Named auth profiles.  Each one is a name, a runtime, and the
     environment variable that holds the token.  The token is not in
     this file.  *Note Profiles::.

‘sessions/PROJECT/ID/summary.json’
     The session's model, status, totals, plan flag, schedules that are
     still waiting, its todo list, and its latest review.

‘sessions/PROJECT/ID/messages.jsonl’
     The transcript, one JSON object per line.  A finding from another
     live session is one of those lines.  *Note Messages::.

‘sessions/PROJECT/ID/plan.md’
     The plan, when plan mode has written one.

‘sessions/_detached/ID/’
     A chat with no project.

‘tasks/ID.json’
     One headless task.  *Note Headless::.

‘teams/RIG.json’
     One rig: its pods, its seats, its edges, the session occupying each
     seat, the work each seat still holds, the text sent to each seat,
     the rig's chatroom, a pace that walks context into a seat, and a
     queue row of owned work that can be claimed, noted, closed, handed
     to another seat, or parked on one wake.  The same file holds intake
     that nobody owns yet.  It also holds a declared workflow.  Closing
     its current step opens the next step.  It also holds watchdog jobs
     that remain after Emacs restarts.  It also holds the recap written
     when a seat is handed to a successor.  The seat keeps its name, its
     edges, and its inbound work.  The same file also holds the notice
     written when a seat near its context wall is compacted on purpose,
     and the room line that tells the rest of the team.  The transcript
     summary is ‘M-x harmless-compact’.  *Note Team::.

‘teams/snapshots/RIG/NAME.json’
     A named snapshot of that rig.  The report says, per seat, whether
     it resumed, was rebuilt, started fresh, is waiting on a decision,
     or failed.  A fresh start is a choice.  Checking the snapshot does
     not write.  Restoring writes the rig back only when no seat failed.
     *Note Team::.

‘teams/images/RIG/NAME.json’
     A captured seat.  The live rig is unchanged by the capture.
     Starting a seat from it copies the role and the inbound work and
     leaves the session empty.  Nothing is started.  *Note Team::.

‘teams/packets/RIG/NAME.json’
     What a seat knows.  The live rig is unchanged by the capture.
     Applying it keeps the seat name and binds a session that is already
     running, with a different runtime.  *Note Team::.

‘worktrees/REPOSITORY/NAME/’
     An isolated checkout of that repository.  *Note Worktrees::.

‘memory/global/’
‘memory/workspaces/PROJECT/’
     Notes.  *Note Memory::.

‘computer/’
     Screenshots from ‘computer_screenshot’.  *Note Computer use::.

   PROJECT in a session path is the project directory encoded as one
file name, not the project name you see in the buffer.

   The log is not a file.  It is the buffer ‘*harmless-log*’.  *Note
Trouble::.


