32 Manual
*********

This book is an Info manual.  Open it with ‘M-x harmless-info’, with ‘h’
in a Harmless buffer, or with ‘h’ in the Harmless menu.  After Harmless
has loaded, ‘C-h i’ lists it in the Emacs directory.

   The source is ‘doc/harmless.texi’ next to ‘lisp’.  The file Emacs
reads is ‘doc/harmless.info’.  Rebuild it from the repository root:

     make manual

   That needs ‘makeinfo’, from the Texinfo package.  Commit both the
Texinfo source and the generated Info file.  A change to a command, a
key, a tool, or a permission belongs in the manual in the same change.


